[] Scare monster:
[]
[] If you drop it and step on it, it is like a permanent Elbereth: you can
[] fight all you want without them ever hitting back. If you drop it in a
[] corridor they will not cross it.
[]
[] Every time you drop/pick up a scroll of scare monster it moves toward
[] a cursed state. Drop a blessed scroll, pick it up it is uncursed. Drop
[] that uncursed scroll, pick it up it is cursed. Drop that cursed scroll,
[] pick it up it turns to dust. If you pick up a scroll that turns to dust
[] it is a worn out scare monster scroll.

ohhh, ever so close (and very observant!)

picking up a blessed one will make it uncursed.  bless it again to
be able to re-use it repeatedly.

picking up an uncursed one will merely mark it as being touched as it
wouldn't be fair to make it cursed.  unfortunately, this creates one
of those rare situations were two seemingly identical objects (uncursed
scrolls of scare monster where one is "touched") won't merge in your
inventory.  there's a small bug here (i believe) in that dropping a
"touched" uncursed scare monster scroll on an "untouched" uncursed scare
monster will cause the "untouched" scroll to become "touched", hence when
you go to pick it up it turns to dust.  a rare occurence anyway ...

